title: EMR Connect › Connected systems › What each status means
route: /emr
intro: Every system on the list is in one of three states. Each state shows different buttons and text, and a system moves between them by the clicks on the arrows.
dir: TD
also: In the demo only the seeded Billing system starts in 'Needs attention'. Nothing in the demo moves a Connected system into it. A system that is not Connected also says that New case cannot pull a chart from it.
---
start s0 "Open EMR Connect\nThe two clinical record sites start Connected, the Billing system starts amber"
click n1 "Click 'Connect a system', pass the test, click 'Connect {name}'"
ext n2 "Production: the read-only sign-in expires or the EMR changes its screens\nDemo: only the seeded Billing system starts here"

group gC "Connected"
  store sc "Connected\nGreen pill"
  process c1 "Row: 'Last sync 6 min ago' or 'Syncing', '0 sync failures', what it reads\nButtons: Sync now (dimmed while any sync runs), Manage\nNew case can pull a chart from it"
  process c2 "Synced by 'Sync now' in the card header\nCounts in the Last sync figure"
endgroup

group gA "Needs attention"
  store sa "Needs attention\nAmber pill"
  process a1 "Row: the issue, 'First step: renew the sign-in with Fix.' and 'New case cannot pull a chart from it until it is connected.'\nShows its missed syncs, for example '2 sync failures'\nButtons: Fix, Manage\nThe 'Action required' line names it"
  process a2 "Skipped by 'Sync now'\nStill counts in the Last sync figure"
endgroup

group gD "Disconnected"
  store sd "Disconnected\nRed pill"
  process d1 "Row: 'Not syncing', 'Sync paused', 'Charts from this system are not arriving.' and 'New case cannot pull a chart from it until it is connected.'\nButtons: Reconnect, Manage\nThe 'Action required' line names it"
  process d2 "Skipped by 'Sync now'\nIgnored by the Last sync figure\nThe Manage drawer ends with 'Reconnect'\nIf it was disconnected while it needed attention, the row adds 'Reconnect starts with a fix.'"
endgroup

goto g1 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Connect a system › Choose the system and contact"
goto g2 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Problems › Fix a system that needs attention"
goto g3 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Manage › Disconnect and reconnect"

s0 --> sc & sa
n1 --> sc
n1 -.-> g1
n2 -.-> sa
sc --> c1 --> c2
sa --> a1 --> a2
sd --> d1 --> d2
sa -->|Click 'Fix', then 'Finish and reconnect'| sc
sa -.-> g2
sc -->|Manage, then 'Disconnect', then 'Disconnect'| sd
sa -->|Manage, then 'Disconnect', then 'Disconnect'| sd
sd -->|Click 'Reconnect', fix first if it needed one, then the connection test passes| sc
sd -.-> g3
